{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-8-6","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：连比例与比例与整数","englishTitle":"If there be as many numbers as we please in continued proportion, and the first do not measure the second, neither will any other measure any other.","book":8,"number":6,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":6,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","contentId":"euclid-8-6","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"01e82ff79f8160a7e0ec093145f9d1401d2f3bebb8a943eed30e992bbd407f01","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-8-6.statement","euclid-8-6.construction.1","euclid-8-6.proof.1","euclid-8-6.proof.2","euclid-8-6.proof.3","euclid-8-6.proof.4","euclid-8-6.proof.5","euclid-8-6.proof.6","euclid-8-6.proof.7","euclid-8-6.proof.8","euclid-8-6.conclusion","euclid-8-6.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-8-6.statement","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b13a65a94631dcbaf4786b7051f03a850d8ad0bdb30ae0c6da1751a0da303d5c","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If there be as many numbers as we please in continued proportion, and the first do not measure the second, neither will any other measure any other."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果连比例我们想多留几个数字,而第一个数字不是整除,第二个数字,其他整除也不会。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"c22862cf8731b00ea965dcb0fce034d385d643673e897d50a4a6dab6abc2656d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Let there be as many numbers as we please, A, B, C, D, E, in continued proportion, and let A not measure B; I say that neither will any other measure any other."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让我们想多少就多少,A,B,C,D,E,连比例,A,而不是整除,B;我说,任何其他整除也不会。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"412e5ac254219a0cd7d5c269f4e9590de0ce2f6402b242e2310523b52abc6d53","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now it is manifest that A, B, C, D, E do not measure one another in order; for A does not even measure B."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,显然A,B,C,D,E没有相互排列整除;A甚至没有整除,B。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"748055f474240fb37cd07d2aa50ab0c82104ea44541499b4948ad0270a68d8ba","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"I say, then, that neither will any other measure any other."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"我说,那么, 任何其他整除也不会了。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e03a007e44526c704563e1761d372859332423e535caf0ef9ecc39278e700134","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let A measure C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,A 整除 C。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"76514865d5b99cd26c0992c2e65283746fbe8698af8466ce3bf5c14505fd871e","citations":["euclid-7-33"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, however many A, B, C are, let as many numbers F, G, H, the least of those which have the same ratio with A, B, C, be taken. [[VII. 33](/principles/euclid-7-33)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"A, B, C以F、G、H等数字计算,在A、B、C这一比相同者中,最少者为A、H。 [[VII. 33](/principles/euclid-7-33)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"70406d9c9f932f30885241d889e183b8b9282b607f4db015f48fe9f725903281","citations":["euclid-7-14"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now, since F, G, H are in the same ratio with A, B, C, and the multitude of the numbers A, B, C is equal to the multitude of the numbers F, G, H, therefore, ex aequali, as A is to C, so is F to H. [[VII. 14](/principles/euclid-7-14)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在,F,G,H与A,B,C的比相同,A,B,C的数目与F,G,H的数目相同,因此,从平等角度讲,A对C的比等于F对H的比；A 与 C 之比等于 F 与 H 之比。 [[VII. 14](/principles/euclid-7-14)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"00b27f82510f527ed14226cc63db16164b1866cdbb765a510fe69487f39c4b8f","citations":["euclid-7-def-20"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And since, as A is to B, so is F to G, while A does not measure B, therefore neither does F measure G; [[VII. Def. 20](/principles/euclid-7-def-20)] therefore F is not an unit, for the unit measures any number."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,A对B的比等于F对G的比。A不是整除 B因此,F 整除 G也没有;因此,F不是单位、单位 整除 任意数字；A 与 B 之比等于 F 与 G 之比。 [[VII. Def. 20](/principles/euclid-7-def-20)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"13a39158e0e693e7947af11c01a192b4f54797cd0a01d07b0addc7595ec21512","citations":["euclid-8-3"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Now F, H are prime to one another. [[VIII. 3](/principles/euclid-8-3)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"现在F,H是互素。 [[VIII. 3](/principles/euclid-8-3)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b9f20fb613960a2f9a28f072b109c4e05581fdea5904b417f6de21b14819d4b3","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, as F is to H, so is A to C; therefore neither does A measure C."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"F比H等于A比C,因此A比整除、C也等于A比C；F 与 H 之比等于 A 与 C 之比。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":10,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a914f6bdfa2ae6c87366a824a5c6a87e2f2baa8386f358d2a670960e5d5e88b8","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Similarly we can prove that neither will any other measure any other. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,我们可以证明,其他整除也不可能。 证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-8-6.source","contentId":"euclid-8-6","revisionId":"euclid-8-6@raw-01e82ff79f8160a7","order":11,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"575627605daf3895cd25f69906d5020ef31fb8cecd3276acb5d1002ba2dfd718","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-8-6:euclid-7-33:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-6","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-6.proof.4"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-33","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.prop.6/","sourceLabel":"VII. 33"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-8-6:euclid-7-14:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-8-6","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-8-6.proof.5"],"targetContentId":"euclid-7-14","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:8.pr